WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.301 line:0%
-You guys, we don't always
have enough time

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.503 line:0%
to cover all
the recent news.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.337 line:0%
So, here with a recap
is one of our writers,

00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:10.476 line:0%
Amber Ruffin, in a segment
we call "Amber Says What?"

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:13.179 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.681
-[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:17.349
Things have been crazy.

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:20.687
Okay, first of all,
a rapper named Lil Nas X

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.423
released a country song
called "Old Town Road."

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:27.293
And I was like, "What? No one
wants to hear a country song."

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.728
Then, I listened to it,
and was like,

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:32.231
"What? This is my new favorite
country song."

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:35.001
And Billboard was like,
"This isn't a country song."

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.637
And I was like,
"What would you call this?"

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:41.007
-♪ I take my horse
to the old town road ♪

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:44.643
♪ I'm gonna ride
till I can't no more ♪

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:46.913
-♪ I got the horses
in the back ♪

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.547
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:50.750
-Yeah!
Oh, my God!

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.687
It is such
a good song!

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.790
I wonder why they won't
count it as country.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.661
We....may....never...know.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.796
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.332
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.734
Then, Billy Ray Cyrus
was like,

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:11.004
"I know how to get it
on the country charts.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.306
I'll do a remix."
And he did.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:16.309
And Billboard was like, "This
is still not a country song."

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:19.946
And I was like, "Dang.
That [bleep] runs deep."

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.914
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.750
Also, Gayle King
interviewed R. Kelly.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.018
I was like, "What?"

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.853
Then, in the middle
of the interview,

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:30.356
he lost his mind,
and started yelling.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.824
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.092
Check it out.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.262
-[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.330
-Robert.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.932
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:42.068
She was like, "Robert."

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.169
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.537
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.106
She hit him with
such a good "Robert"

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:52.011
that I sat up straight --
and my name is not even Robert.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:55.248
Then, I saw the first-ever
picture taken of a black hole.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.683
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.585
Then, I heard the scientist

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.686
in charge of getting
that picture was a woman,

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.555
and I was like, "What?"

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:06.826
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:12.098
Then, I got so excited I tweeted
a bunch of dirty jokes about it.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:15.034
And then, my mom saw them,
and I got in trouble.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.368
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:18.204
And that's a true story.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.305
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.639
And then, I was like,
"You know what?

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:22.041
Those jokes
weren't that bad."

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.811
But then, I looked at them
again, and they kind of were.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:28.848
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.882
Hey, mom!

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.185
Then,
Beyonce announced --

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.853
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:37.056
Then, Beyonce announced that
she'll release a documentary

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:40.326
of her Coachella performance
on April 17th.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.761
And I was like, "What!?"

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.964
I got so excited
that I planned a viewing party.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.999
Oh, that reminds me --
Seth?

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:49.435
-Yeah?
-I need the 17th off.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:52.271
-No. Just watch it at your desk
like everyone else.

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.573
-Abuse!

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.341
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.109
Anyway,
party at my desk.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.677
So, let's see.
What else happened?

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:02.314
Oh. Beto O'Rourke keeps putting
his shoes on countertops

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:03.483
all over the country.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.518
And I'm like,
"What?

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.186
Get down from there.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.588
Someone has to
clean that."

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.657
Unless he wins
the Democratic nomination.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.894
Then, I'll be like,
"What...a genius."

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.463
I love how he puts his shoes
on everything.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:21.534
Then, I saw Grace Jones,
who is 70 years old,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.570
dance down the runway at the
Tommy Hilfiger fashion show.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.605
And I was like,
"What?"

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:30.176
This woman is
70 years old!

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.879
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.080
Yeah.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.449
Now, usually,
when a 70-year-old

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:40.153
dances around with no pants on,
her kids take away her car keys.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.387
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.755
Not this supermodel.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.724
Now, how can she look this good
at this age?

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:49.895
I know I say it a lot,
but blackness cannot be cracked.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.763
You cannot crack it.

00:03:51.763 --> 00:03:53.932
Freeze it.
Drop it from a building.

00:03:53.932 --> 00:03:58.571
Nary a crack shall appear,
for it is the uncrackable.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:01.608
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.280
I'm 60 years old.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.681
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:11.184
I heard the worst thing
in the world.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.518
Now, this is true.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:16.856
A woman in Taiwan had four bees
living under her eyelid,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.224
living off of her tears!

00:04:19.224 --> 00:04:21.660
I read that article.
I was like, "What?!"

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.264
So, just to be safe --
for any bees out there,

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:27.066
my tears are
made of poison.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.435
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.371
Oh, dang it!

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:33.372
Oh!

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.574
I should have done this.
Go back.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:38.678
♪ My tears are poison ♪

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.713
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:46.285
How did I miss that?!

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:47.420
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.156
-Ooh, that was
a close one.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:52.257
Then, I heard --
-I won the bet!

00:04:52.257 --> 00:04:54.427
-Ah!

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.729
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:04:56.729 --> 00:05:00.065
I heard that they dropped the
charges against Jussie Smollett

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:02.901
for wasting everyone's time
by calling in a fake crime.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:05.771
And I was like, "What?
He's not gonna get in trouble

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:07.372
for reporting
a fake crime?

00:05:07.372 --> 00:05:10.643
What is he --
a white woman?"

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.680
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.819
All these white women
are like, "Yeah."

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:20.953
Then...

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.054
Then, in...

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:23.689
[ Laughs ]

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:27.226
Then, in Harry Potter news,
J.K. Rowling was like,

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:31.797
"Dumbledore and Grindelwald had
an intense sexual relationship."

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:36.068
And I was like, "What?
What is wrong with you?

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:39.705
Who asked for this?
And why did you do that?

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:43.409
And when can I read about it
in detail?"

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.945
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.213
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:48.213 --> 00:05:49.649
I like what I like.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:53.552
Then, I heard a rhino poacher
got trampled by an elephant

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:56.889
and then eaten by lions
on an animal preserve.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:06:00.559
And I was like, "What?
Oh, good idea, animals."

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:02.695
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.600
"Work together,
like y'all do in the cartoons.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.436
[Bleep] if those birds
can make Cinderella a dress,

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.038
you can stop poaching."

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.072
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:15.474
This has been
"Amber Says What?"

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:18.845
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:26.018 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.953
-Amber Ruffin, everybody.

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:28.988
There she is.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.389
We'll be right back.

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:31.924
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

